/*
    `contract` requires the implementation on the left to be a member of the function set
    on the right. It is left-declarative: the new frame is declarative over the
    implementation and referential over the contract expression, so the contract can
    refer to argument and result declarations collected from the nested function.
    The value is the implementation paired with its opaque external description: a
    separately compiled consumer sees only the contract, never the body.
    Contracts compose with the ordinary set operators, e.g. `float ^^ float & NonZeroArg`.
*/

(float x => 1.0 / x) contract (float ^^ float)
